MUNICIPALITY OF PINOS (SOLSONÈS). 
Do you know where the geographical center of Catalonia is? 
- Discover the exact point that divides the Catalan territory and everything that surrounds it. 
 
The geographical center of Catalonia is a place as curious as little known by many. Located in the municipality of Pinós, in the Solsonès region, this special point is located near the Pinós Sanctuary, an emblematic space that combines history, nature and spirituality. If you have never wondered where the heart of our territory is, it is in this location that the exact coordinates that divide Catalonia equidistantly converge. 
 
The landscape that surrounds the geographical center of Catalonia is marked by the beauty of the rural environment and the contrasts that explain the geographical and human history of this area. In 1998, a devastating fire ravaged much of the municipality, leaving an indelible mark on the territory. However, the regeneration of nature has been gaining ground, making space an example of resilience. Today, visitors can enjoy a scenery that combines mountains, forests and charming paths. 
 
- A strategic and emblematic point. 
Pinós, a municipality formed by five nuclei – Ardèvol, Vallmanya, Sant Just d’Ardèvol, Pinós and Matamargó –, is known for its peculiar strategic location. The central part of the term is presented as a backbone with altitudes between 700 and 800 meters, structuring the Llobregat and Segre basins. This is a privileged natural observation point, where the relief seems to have been shaped to offer unbeatable panoramic views. 
 
The highlight of this area is the Sierra de Pinós, with 930.6 meters of altitude. This is, without a doubt, a place that invites exploration, whether on foot, by bicycle or simply enjoying the silence and tranquility that characterize this unique place. 
 
In addition to its geographical interest in being the center of Catalonia, the municipality is rich in historical and cultural heritage. The Sanctuary of Pinós is one of the great attractions of the area, not only for being a point of pilgrimage, but also for its architecture and connection with the religious past of the region. For those who enjoy the local gastronomy, the offer of typical products also makes the visit worth the visit. 
 
- A landscape that tells a story. 
One of Pinós’ most fascinating aspects is how the landscape tells a story of overcoming. The forests burned during the fires of the nineties have been replaced by vegetation that has returned to take root with force, offering today a natural spectacle that changes with the seasons. The green tones of spring give way to the golden colors of autumn, making each visit to this place unique. 
 
This area is also a witness to the strong link between nature and the people of the region. With a lifestyle based on agriculture, livestock farming and sustainable tourism, the inhabitants of Pinós have been able to adapt to the challenges of the territory, keeping alive a heritage that is an essential part of Catalan identity. 
 
- The Catalan epicenter. 
If you are looking for a different place, full of history, spirituality and nature, the geographical center of Catalonia awaits you with open arms. A visit to Pinós will not only allow you to discover the exact point that divides the Catalan territory, but will also give you the opportunity to connect with the essence of a land that knows how to captivate with its beauty and authenticity. 
